{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/605571-wyrmcomer`s-meaning","id":605571,"title":"Wyrmcomer`s Meaning","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-28T07:36:59-07:00","id":605571,"title":"Wyrmcomer`s Meaning","content":"Hello! ^^<br /> <br /> As spanish is my mother tongue, I have some difficulties understanding the specific meaning behind this word &quot;Wyrmcomer&quot;. I'm debating with my friends and we've come to conclussion that it must be one of these:<br /> <br /> - &quot;Those who came when the Wyrm did&quot; or &quot;with the Wyrm&quot; (as Wyrmcomer sounds like Newcomer)<br /> - &quot;Those who wear the Wyrm with them&quot; (we argued that if so, they could have been Wyrmbringers or Wyrmbearers, too)<br /> - &quot;Those who are harbingers of the Wyrm&quot;<br /> <br /> Can you please help us? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7066-gsabinescu","user":"GSabinescu","date":". 07-28-2015, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7066-gsabinescu","name":"GSabinescu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T07:45:50-07:00","id":605598,"title":"","content":"I usually take it to mean the first one, that they arrived with the Wyrm (though technically, there was still quite a lot of Wyrm before them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T08:58:01-07:00","id":605636,"title":"","content":"There's a few nice nuances that all orbit around the same concept. They brought the Wyrm with them; Their coming presaged the Wyrm's arrival; etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T09:25:06-07:00","id":605647,"title":"","content":"I've always interpreted it as meaning &quot;Those that brought The Wyrm with them&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T09:26:28-07:00","id":605649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/605571-wyrmcomer`s-meaning?p=605647#post605647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always interpreted it as meaning &quot;Those that brought The Wyrm with them&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more Wyrmbringer, which is what they call the non-Garou and Kin Europeans. Wyrmcomer is what they called the European Garou and their Kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T09:57:20-07:00","id":605668,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I always thought those terms were interchangeable, and just depended on the speaker and what kind of tone he wanted to achieve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T10:59:31-07:00","id":605706,"title":"","content":"It's just an insulting neologism, so all answers are true with added bitterness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T20:31:28-07:00","id":606302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GSabinescu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/605571-wyrmcomer`s-meaning#post605571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As spanish is my mother tongue, I have some difficulties understanding the specific meaning behind this word &quot;Wyrmcomer&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is vague in English too. It is meant to be able to have multiple meanings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GSabinescu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/605571-wyrmcomer`s-meaning#post605571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- &quot;Those who came when the Wyrm did&quot; or &quot;with the Wyrm&quot; (as Wyrmcomer sounds like Newcomer)<br /> - &quot;Those who wear the Wyrm with them&quot; (we argued that if so, they could have been Wyrmbringers or Wyrmbearers, too)<br /> - &quot;Those who are harbingers of the Wyrm&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>All of these are possible meanings. It is likely the phrase is meant to imply any of those depending on context and intent. &quot;Officially&quot; Wyrmcomers means they who came when the Wyrm did, but it also implies they came with the Wyrm (they brought it with them). I've also seen &quot;Wyrmbringers&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T10:01:07-07:00","id":606740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/605571-wyrmcomer`s-meaning?p=605649#post605649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's more Wyrmbringer, which is what they call the non-Garou and Kin Europeans. Wyrmcomer is what they called the European Garou and their Kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is the distinction between &quot;Wyrmbringers&quot; (what the Uktena and Wendigo call &quot;white people&quot; [when they're not calling them &quot;wasichu&quot;] because they brought the Wyrm with them when they arrived in the New World) and &quot;Wyrmcomers&quot; (which is what the Uktena and Wendigo call the other Garou tribes because they &quot;came here when the Wyrm came here.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Essentially:<br /> <br /> White people = wasichu = Wyrmbringers<br /> <br /> while<br /> <br /> Non-Uktena/Wendigo Garou = Wyrmcomers<br /> <br /> I don't remember which book this is detailed in, but this is the right distinction between Wyrmbringer and Wyrmcomer. Trust me, you might annoy a non-native Garou if you call him a Wyrmcomer, which just means that his tribe arrived at the same time as the Wyrm in the New World. But you <i>will </i>piss him off if you call him a Wyrmbringer, which all but states outright that he <i>colluded in</i> bringing the Wyrm to the New World, which is almost the same as accusing him of being a Black Spiral Dancer. Yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 07-29-2015, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 20